      "description": "Yoked menus are anchored to the active run's recorded offsets from a single operator-start anchor, so the active run's operator boundary pause becomes part of the yoked schedule. A yoked boundary Resume later than the active pause (here 4.09 s vs 2.95 s) puts the next menu's anchor in the past; the item faults MENU_REPLAY_ANCHOR_MISSED and every later Resume re-faults with the same code, so the visit cannot recover."
